    "result_text": "BUILD SUCCESS \u2014 the full suite is green.\n\nThe change is complete. Here's what I did, following the codebase's established `bulkSignupWarning` pattern (a transient field computed by a pipeline step and read by the mapper):\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a transient `householdSize` field (owners sharing the same `householdId`, counting this owner), never persisted.\n\n2. **`AssignOwnerHouseholdSize.java`** (new function) \u2014 counts owners sharing the owner's `householdId` (a lone owner with no household counts as 1) and records it as `householdSize`.\n\n3. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted the `householdSize` step after `warn` (post-Save, so the new owner is counted).\n\n4. **`owners/{ownerId}.GET.yml`** \u2014 inserted the same step so a later GET recomputes the identical value.\n\n5. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 `membershipTier` now yields `GOLD` when `householdSize >= 3`, otherwise the existing SILVER/BRONZE rules apply.\n\n6. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `GOLD` to the `membershipTier` enum and updated its description (this regenerates `OwnerDto.MembershipTierEnum.GOLD`).\n\nThe acceptance test `coreGoldForThreeMemberHousehold` and the full suite pass.",
